The rainbows I like best aren't the big, grand ones that stretch across the whole sky. I love the tiny, shy ones that appear in the spray of a garden hose on a sunny afternoon. You have to stand just right to see them, a little arc of colour dancing in the water drops.

I also love the ones you see in a puddle after a storm. A smear of rainbow, all mixed up with the mud and the fallen leaves. It’s like the sky has left a little bit of its magic behind for us to find.

But my very favourite is the one that comes after a really heavy downpour, when the sun bursts out and the world smells of wet grass. It’s so bright and clear, and it always makes me feel like everything is going to be all right. It’s a promise of a better day. [end of text]


